OL,3,GNEWSAYoung striker backs city's
OL,4,Aanti-vaping campaign
OL,5,
OL,6,FBradford City striker Harry Ibbitson
OL,7,Fhas backed a campaign to persuade the
OL,8,Fcity's young people not to take up
OL,9,Fvaping.
OL,11,FCatch Your Breath is being promoted by
OL,12,Fthe club's community foundation
OL,13,Falongside Bradford Council and is
OL,14,Fcoming to the end of a 12-month run.
OL,16,FIbbitson, 20, was among a group of
OL,17,Fpeople who met at the club's main
OL,18,Ftraining ground at Apperley Bridge on
OL,19,FMonday to talk about the initiative.
OL,23,APub: 17-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
